IMPORT prelude

-- A two-party contract for the instance ledger's MCP write tools
-- (OPERATIONAL-LOWERING-SPEC section 9, WPO6; D-O13). An operational-
-- lowering fixture only, written for those tools' tests.
--
-- Alice quotes a price with a note, and Bob answers within the day by
-- accepting it. Each obligation names the party who must perform it, and
-- each act is named in the obligation by its constructor, so an MCP caller
-- who is Alice is offered the quote and none of Bob's acts, and one who
-- is Bob the reverse. The dinner fixtures cannot show that: every one of
-- their acts is by World (companion REGULATIVE-LOWERING-SPEC, option C).
--
-- The quote carries a NUMBER and a STRING and Bob's acceptance a BOOLEAN,
-- the three field types a write tool takes. Two acts get no write tool,
-- and are never performed in the tests: `Alice asks to see the terms` has
-- a field of a list type, and `Alice files a reference` has a field named
-- like one of the write tool's own arguments (idempotencyKey).

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Alice, Bob

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `Alice quotes`
        HAS price IS A NUMBER
            note IS A STRING
    `Bob accepts`
        HAS agreed IS A BOOLEAN
    `Alice asks to see the terms`
        HAS clauses IS A LIST OF STRING
    `Alice files a reference`
        HAS idempotencyKey IS A STRING

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the exchange` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MUST `Alice quotes` price note
    WITHIN 86400
    HENCE `Bob answers`
    LEST BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Bob answers` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MUST `Bob accepts` agreed
    WITHIN 86400
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice may ask` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MAY `Alice asks to see the terms` clauses
    WITHIN 86400
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice may file` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MAY `Alice files a reference` idempotencyKey
    WITHIN 86400
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED
